# Day 1 — Channel Four. 21 August. Arrive at 15:30; the walk up; the first radio check.
# On Day 1 Dot ends every transmission with "over".

call D1_ARRIVE
  day 1
  time 15:00-26:00
  where cab until 17:00
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Radio check, over.
choice
  > "Basin, Kestrel. Loud and clear." -> clear
  > "Hello? Is this... hello?" -> hello
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node clear
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Loud and clear.
DOT  Well. Look at you. Augie took three days to say it right. Over.
goto job
node hello
THEO Hello? Is this... hello?
DOT  It's a radio, Kestrel, not a seance.
DOT  Push, talk, let go, listen. Most people get the last part wrong. Over.
goto job
node quiet
DOT  ...Kestrel? You push the button, you talk, you let go. Try again, over.
choice
  > "Basin, Kestrel. Loud and clear." -> clear
  > "Hello? Is this... hello?" -> hello
  > [say nothing] -> nod
node nod
DOT  Okay. I'll take that as a nod. Over.
node job
DOT  Welcome to Kestrel. Kettle sticks — hit it on the left side.
DOT  Get settled. I'll call you this evening with the rest of it. Basin out.

call D1_PM
  day 1
  time 19:30-26:00
  after D1_ARRIVE
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You got time for the job description? Over.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Go ahead.
DOT  Look at the horizon now and then. You see smoke, you sight it in the finder — the big round thing in the middle of your room — and you call me with a bearing.
DOT  Readings morning and evening from the white box on the catwalk. Write it all in the log.
DOT  And otherwise, Kestrel, you are paid to sit. Augie was very, very good at it. Twenty-two years. Over.
choice
  > "That's it? Sit and look?" -> thatsit
  > "He left things here. Notes." -> things
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node thatsit
THEO That's it? Sit and look?
DOT  Sit and look and listen. People think it's the easy part. People are wrong about a lot of things. Over.
goto out
node things
THEO He left things here. Notes. A kettle with opinions.
DOT  He leaves everyone things. You'll find more. He was a terrible speller and a very good man. Over.
goto out
node quiet
DOT  You'll get used to the quiet. Or you won't, and that's a different conversation. Over.
node out
DOT  Basin out.

call D1_NIGHT
  day 1
  time 21:00-26:00
  after D1_PM
  kind small
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. One more thing and then I'll let you sleep. Over.
DOT  You'll hear the tower talking tonight. Ticks, knocks. It's the wood cooling. Don't answer it. Over.
choice
  > "Goodnight, Basin." -> night
  > "What if it says something interesting?" -> interesting
  > [say nothing] -> quiet
node night
THEO Goodnight, Basin.
DOT  Goodnight, Kestrel. Basin out.
end
node interesting
THEO What if it says something interesting?
DOT  Then write it down. That's what the logbook's for. Goodnight, Kestrel. Over.
end
node quiet
DOT  ...Goodnight, Kestrel. Over.
